entries.pseudocode:
INPUT: none (runs standalone in <head>)
OUTPUT: html data-theme applied before first paint — zero-flash
ERRORS: any exception -> data-theme='light' (safe default), execution continues
SNIPPET (ships inside <head>, BEFORE the stylesheet link and before any body markup, render-blocking by position):
<script>
(function () {
  var m;
  try { m = localStorage.getItem('theme_mode'); } catch (e) { m = null; }
  if (m !== 'system' && m !== 'light' && m !== 'dark') { m = 'light'; }
  if (m === 'system') {
    document.documentElement.removeAttribute('data-theme');
  } else {
    document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', m);
  }
})();
</script>
1. Head parses -> snippet executes synchronously -> attribute state settled BEFORE body/content paints.
2. Explicit stored mode -> attribute set on frame 1 (saved dark never shows a light frame; saved light never shows a dark frame).
3. System stored -> attribute left absent; the @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) block decides tokens at first paint (no flash either way).
4. try/catch maps any storage failure to the Light default — the page never boots unthemed.
5. No external script, no framework, no network fetch — inline vanilla JS only (D40 offline rule).
